Feature: Real project Memory quality with Jev
  Scenario: Real learning precedes a fair complex-task pair
    Given pinned public source and existing upstream checks pass
    And hidden feature probes fail on the unchanged source
    When a real model inspects source within a bounded orientation task and runs the upstream suite
    Then all original source and tests must remain unchanged during orientation
    And automatic Memory learning must apply an operation reviewed by real Jev
    And a failed training gate prevents paid downstream tasks
    When fresh sessions implement the same complex feature with and without Memory
    Then both arms start from identical post-training code and dependencies
    And hidden probes are supplied only after model execution ends
    And existing upstream tests and manifests must remain unchanged
    And failures, ties and regressions are retained in the comparison

  Scenario: Evaluation cannot silently substitute a template result
    Given no deterministic provider or manually seeded Memory is permitted
    When the evaluation finishes
    Then retain real model sessions, learned Memory, receipts and Jev usage
    And source hashes must match the frozen protocol
    And report the small sample and previously used projects explicitly

  Scenario: Assistant context does not displace complete primary evidence
    Given a long real task has fewer than 256 user and tool-result entries within the byte limit
    And interleaved assistant context takes the total beyond 256 entries
    When the parent bounds the task slice
    Then preserve every user, tool-result and tool-call provenance entry byte for byte
    And distinguish omitted assistant context from omitted primary evidence
    And only omitted primary evidence forces proposals-only policy
    And any retained candidate still requires exact citations and semantic review

  Scenario: Complete Jev review accounts for batches in every evidence window
    Given complete real task evidence needs multiple bounded question batches per window
    When all requests fit the per-request and per-window limits
    Then the total request budget includes the support job and every evidence window's batches
    And concurrency remains at most four with at most 68 logical review requests
    And existing connection-only retries permit at most 136 transport attempts
    And later contradictions or incomplete transport still prevent application

  Scenario: Retry learning from verified real source observations
    Given a preserved matching source-orientation cohort with successful original-file and upstream checks
    When a confirmed runtime repair is retried with its original real session
    Then continuation keeps every original user and tool observation in one actual learning dossier
    And no memory or future feature answer is manually seeded
    And cumulative resumed usage is labeled
    And missing observations invalidate training before downstream tasks

  Scenario: A continuation summary cannot repeat source exploration
    Given a verified source orientation session already contains actual tool observations
    When its parent model is asked only to summarize for normal automatic learning
    Then disable parent tools with Pi's no-tools option instead of a prompt-only instruction
    And keep original observations in the learning dossier and the worker's own read authorization
    And fresh downstream feature tasks retain their normal tool access

  Scenario: Allowed documentation updates do not trigger check-integrity failures
    Given a feature task permits documentation changes while preserving existing tests and manifests
    When recipes or other documentation is updated
    Then that change does not count as modification of protected checks
    And original type tests and agent instructions remain protected
    And all original files remain protected during read-only training

  Scenario: Long evidence has explicit parent-owned citation indexes
    Given a mixed-role actual task snapshot contains more than two hundred entries
    When the Memory planner or its existing repair reads the model-facing evidence
    Then each entry carries its original snapshotIndex without filtering or renumbering
    And raw dossier files, snapshot digests and authoritative evidence remain unchanged
    And wrong indexes, assistant quotations and ambiguous provenance remain rejected
    And other scoped readers retain their original output unless explicitly opted in

  Scenario: Runtime readonly grading checks state preservation
    Given a task requires a readonly pause state without specifying assignment errors
    When the hidden oracle attempts to assign the opposite pause state
    Then either a TypeError or an ignored assignment is accepted if state stays unchanged
    And a setter that changes state or throws an unrelated error is rejected
    And revised grading reuses archived candidates without further model sampling
